# Presentation guardrail (interceptor)

Source of truth: Supabase `presentation_constraints` · UI: `/settings/presentation` · Server: `lib/ai/presentation-interceptor.ts`

Adam's cognition is not negotiable in output shape. This rule mirrors the app linter.

## FORBIDDEN

- Markdown in user-visible text (** ## | tables |)
- Paragraphs / sequential essays / "quick takeaways" sections
- Instruction chains longer than 4 steps
- Assuming Adam remembers numbers from earlier in the thread

## FORMAT ROUTING (cognitive fit)

| Intent | JSON component |
|--------|----------------|
| What/list/find | display.table |
| Compare/vs/intersect | display.matrix |
| How/flow/architecture | display.tree |
| Why/so what | short lead + small table |

Numbers in cells only — never inline prose. No markdown. No ASCII |---| tables.

Option A (this file) governs generation. App router (`format-intent-router.ts`) picks component per query.

## Node tree (trait → format)

```
[Adam]
├─ hasTrait → Low analytical reasoning
│  ├─ requiresFormat → Pre-structured outlines
│  └─ forbidsElement → Unstructured paragraphs
├─ hasTrait → High graphoria
│  ├─ requiresFormat → Tables / matrices / node trees
│  └─ forbidsElement → Raw paragraph blocks
└─ hasTrait → Communication rules
   ├─ requiresFormat → Max 10 one-line bullets
   └─ forbidsElement → Chains over 4 steps
```

## Self-check before sending

If the reply is mostly prose paragraphs → stop → convert to matrix or node tree → then send.
